{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Ed8qHPVJ9FaAPGrsQKVsW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found and read all the source files. Here's my comprehensive report:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Definition\n\nThe `DiffTest` struct is defined in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5182/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` at lines 46-55. Here are all the fields with their types:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `Name` | `string` | Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run) |\n| `Args` | `[]string` | Command-line arguments passed to both binaries |\n| `Stdin` | `[]byte` | Input stream; nil means EOF immediately; empty slice `[]byte{}` means open stdin immediately closed |\n| `Env` | `[]string` | Environment variables as KEY=VALUE pairs; nil means inherit test process environment with LC_ALL=C applied |\n| `WorkDir` | `string` | Working directory for test execution |\n| `ExitCode` | `int` | Expected exit code (defaults to 0 when zero value) |\n| `Normalize` | `[]NormalizeFunc` | Slice of normalization functions applied in order to stdout/stderr before comparison |\n| `ExpectedFiles` | `map[string][]byte` | Files expected to be created during test execution, mapped by relative path |\n\n## RunDiffTests Function\n\nThe `RunDiffTests` function is located at lines 83-90 in `difftest.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tfor _, tc := range tests {\n\t\tt.Run(tc.Name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\trunSubtest(t, goBinary, refBinary, tc)\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n## Answers to Your Specific Questions\n\n### 1. Exit Code Handling\n\nExit codes are handled in the `runSubtest` function (lines 92-105) and `compareOutputs` function (lines 176-185):\n- The `runBinary` function extracts exit codes via the `extractResult` function (lines 130-148)\n- If a command succeeds, exit code is 0; if it fails, the code extracts the `ExitError.ExitCode()`\n- In `compareOutputs`, both binaries' exit codes are compared: `exitMatch := goRes.exitCode == refRes.exitCode`\n- If they don't match, the test fails with a formatted divergence message showing both exit codes\n\n### 2. WorkDir Handling\n\nWorkDir handling is in `runSubtest` (lines 92-105):\n```go\nworkDir := tc.WorkDir\nif workDir == \"\" {\n    workDir = t.TempDir()\n}\n```\n- If `WorkDir` is empty, a temporary directory is automatically created via `t.TempDir()`\n- If `WorkDir` is specified, that directory is used as the current working directory for both binaries\n- The working directory is set in `runBinary` via `cmd.Dir = workDir` (line 116)\n\n### 3. Fixture File Setup\n\nThere's **no explicit setup function** like `SetupFunc` in the struct. However, there are two ways to set up fixture files:\n\n1. **Pre-created files in WorkDir**: You can specify a custom `WorkDir` and pre-populate it with files before running the test\n2. **File verification via ExpectedFiles**: After test execution, `checkExpectedFiles` (lines 211-227) verifies that files created during test execution match expected content in the `ExpectedFiles` map\n\nThe `ExpectedFiles` field is checked at the end of `runSubtest` (line 104): `checkExpectedFiles(t, workDir, tc.ExpectedFiles)`\n\n## Additional Utilities\n\nThe package also provides:\n- **TimestampNormalizer** (lines 66-72): A built-in `NormalizeFunc` that replaces common timestamp patterns with `<TIMESTAMP>`\n- **ComposeNormalizers** (lines 232-238): Convenience function to combine multiple normalizers into a single function"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae8391aa-d8b0-470e-b364-c0a8b7c2dcca","uuid":"54da56d0-5613-4a8a-840e-afe23d5a7b7e","timestamp":"2026-05-14T16:29:34.678Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5182, find and read the DiffTest struct d